{:edb/db-before-t 2288 :edb/db-after-t 2289 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535601 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:22:42.296Z" 13194139535601 true] [17592186129096 1020 #edb/ref 17592186356987 13194139535601 true] [17592186129097 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357000 13194139535601 true] [17592186129097 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357014 13194139535601 true] [17592186129098 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357007 13194139535601 true] [17592186129536 1017 #edb/ref 17592186127010 13194139535601 false] [17592186129536 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356994 13194139535601 true] [17592186129536 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535601 true] [17592186129536 1100 "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x, y, z) = e^{-x^{2} - y^{2} - z^{2}}$?" 13194139535601 false] [17592186129536 1100 "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}}?$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186129536 1145 "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {e}^{-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}} & =c \\\\ -{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $0<c\\le 1$ since $-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c$ must be non-negative. If we let $-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c={r}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surfaces form a family of spheres centered at the origin." 13194139535601 true] [17592186356987 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356988 13194139535601 true] [17592186356987 1089 "q-129199" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356987 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535601 true] [17592186356987 1100 "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3}?$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356987 1113 #uuid "252dccd1-3816-5e56-9b75-ae474230a890" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356987 1145 "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {e}^{4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3} & =c \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ z & =4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c>0.$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of elliptic paraboloids:\n\n$$\nz=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c,\\,c\\in (0,\\infty )\n$$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356989 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356990 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356991 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356992 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356993 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1041 "selection" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356989 13194139535601 true] [17592186356988 1110 #uuid "fb381f8a-4bea-53df-91b1-08b8ff021513" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356989 1034 "A family of elliptic paraboloids: $z=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356989 1111 #uuid "cc89d93a-f650-5673-8db9-773c021bc91f" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356990 1034 "A family of elliptic paraboloids: $z=-4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}+3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡c$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356990 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356990 1111 #uuid "bdcd5190-eaef-5b64-bd6c-a01857fc73b1" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356991 1034 "A family of surfaces: $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-c)$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356991 1111 #uuid "bf7146f5-d291-572f-9a8e-ea3d0423858a" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356992 1034 "A family of surfaces: $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3)+c$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356992 1111 #uuid "49c71707-d07d-50a5-8cd5-8e64cc34a1f5" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356993 1034 "A family of hyperboloids of two sheets: ${z}^{2}=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356993 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356993 1111 #uuid "7f36be23-457b-50fb-b93f-741d67d40eb7" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356995 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356996 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356997 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356998 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356999 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1041 "selection" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356997 13194139535601 true] [17592186356994 1110 #uuid "356be647-ae8c-5506-a2f3-4a2451b5dd03" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356995 1034 "A family of spheres centered at $(0,0,{e}^{-1})$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356995 1111 #uuid "45ad949d-4d2e-56aa-84fc-128f042e9a4c" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356996 1034 "A family of spheres centered at $(0,0,e)$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356996 1111 #uuid "8760143c-d921-5b2b-b6ac-21e7470de4c3" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356997 1034 "A family of spheres centered at the origin" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356997 1111 #uuid "4dc7fe16-21b8-5e01-b76d-1c688bcf3c89" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356998 1034 "A family of surfaces given by  ${z}^{2}+c={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $c>0$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356998 1111 #uuid "67290681-9872-5ba5-89b3-941d47ec4615" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356999 1034 "A family of surfaces given by ${z}^{2}+c={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $c\\ne 0$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186356999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535601 true] [17592186356999 1111 #uuid "5e460968-e353-588b-8bdd-a7ff65ccde11" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357000 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357001 13194139535601 true] [17592186357000 1089 "q-37131" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357000 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535601 true] [17592186357000 1100 "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z$ that passes through the point $P(0,1,1).$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357000 1113 #uuid "e3e19cf1-1438-5521-a704-9195b3cd730a" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357000 1145 "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1,1) & =0\\cdot 1+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ xy+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z & =\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-xy \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-xy) \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(0,1,1)$ is the surface $z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy.$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357002 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357003 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357004 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357005 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357006 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1041 "selection" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357005 13194139535601 true] [17592186357001 1110 #uuid "d76830ff-d00f-56aa-9d9d-e9f2e9fc3065" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357002 1034 "z=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357002 1111 #uuid "e8743c70-1eb7-5ec4-8bb9-4c34fe99a98a" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357003 1034 "z=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357003 1111 #uuid "b2899bac-97db-5f57-b481-a04587b7e4b3" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357004 1034 "z=\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357004 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357004 1111 #uuid "7c8c531f-b4c8-5d4a-9e6a-35f135f5ddbe" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357005 1034 "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357005 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357005 1111 #uuid "1c93ce09-8f59-5716-b3af-4b54a575dad3" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357006 1034 "z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357006 1111 #uuid "2e938519-b510-510d-94e1-c33aec43b04b" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357007 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357008 13194139535601 true] [17592186357007 1089 "q-71574" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357007 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535601 true] [17592186357007 1100 "For the function $f(x,y,z)=z-x-y-1,$ find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=1.$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357007 1113 #uuid "e388c922-dab9-5bf6-870c-17599df704f0" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357007 1145 "The level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ z-x-y-1 & =1 \\\\ z & =x+y+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=1$ is the plane $z=x+y+2.$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357009 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357010 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357011 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357012 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357013 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1041 "selection" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357012 13194139535601 true] [17592186357008 1110 #uuid "d14de792-7989-5c5a-9522-c3dfd65b9bda" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357009 1034 "z=x-y+2" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357009 1111 #uuid "2ba6e191-43d8-5547-b6d0-94e14aafed93" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357010 1034 "z=x+y+1" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357010 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357010 1111 #uuid "bb53c6fc-f3a7-5348-aa34-74d8b978b88f" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357011 1034 "z=\\frac{1}{x+y-1}" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357011 1111 #uuid "7d16788d-ca1b-504e-88df-a4c3da7e4151" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357012 1034 "z=x+y+2" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357012 1111 #uuid "0b114a20-d15d-5381-acc8-70cc1ab0618d" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357013 1034 "z=-x-y-1" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357013 1111 #uuid "d307c0a9-2630-56f5-9a70-0a9e9289c484" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357014 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357015 13194139535601 true] [17592186357014 1089 "q-71593" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357014 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535601 true] [17592186357014 1100 "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{z-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{xy}$ that passes through the point $P(1,1,2).$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357014 1113 #uuid "5c696959-b72e-5102-9ec4-acc967980567" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357014 1145 "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1,2) & =\\frac{(2)-(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}}{(1)(1)}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{z-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{xy} & =2 \\\\ z-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2xy \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}+2xy-{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(1,1,2)$ is the surface $z={x}^{2}+2xy-{y}^{2}.$" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357016 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357017 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357018 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357019 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357020 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1041 "selection" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357017 13194139535601 true] [17592186357015 1110 #uuid "932e4ba5-543a-518f-8a15-dc35af72beff" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357016 1034 "z=(x-y)^{2}" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357016 1111 #uuid "2b3793a2-fe4a-5725-99d7-031958909144" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357017 1034 "z={x}^{2}+2xy-{y}^{2}" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357017 1111 #uuid "ed9be010-ebc4-5754-95a3-77841972757d" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357018 1034 "z={y}^{2}+2xy-{x}^{2}" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [17592186357018 1111 #uuid "451901a1-42ae-5cfb-9d27-7c947c9b5508" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357019 1034 "z={x}^{2}-2xy-{y}^{2}" 13194139535601 true] [17592186357019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535601 true] [1759218